## Why This Is Asked

Assesses capability to design edge-friendly 3D pose systems for dynamic outdoor scenes, handling wind-induced blur, occlusion, and rapid adaptation to new bolt geometries with minimal on-device training.

## Key Concepts

- Edge latency and memory constraints on embedded GPUs
- Monocular 3D pose estimation (6-DoF) from moving cameras
- Few-shot on-device adaptation (2-shot)
- Synthetic-to-real transfer with domain randomization
- Robustness to motion blur and lighting variation

## Code Example

```javascript
function fineTuneAdapter(model, supportImages, supportLabels) {
  // tiny adapter fine-tune on-device
  for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    const batch = getBatch(supportImages, supportLabels);
    const loss = model.computeLoss(batch);
    model.backward(loss);
  }
  return model;
}
```

